{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.BringsIsQou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.BringsIsQou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.standardBringsIsQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.standardBringsIsQOU","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L81-L106","doc":"The canonical QOU verification data for Bring's surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.riemann_hurwitz_brings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.riemann_hurwitz_brings","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L74-L79","doc":"Riemann–Hurwitz verification: for a degree-d covering of P¹ by a\ngenus-g curve, 2g − 2 = d(2·0 − 2) + R_tot, i.e. R_tot = 2g − 2 + 2d.\nFor g = 4, d = 4: R_tot = 6 + 8 = 14. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.brings_euler_char_neg_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.brings_euler_char_neg_six","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L67-L72","doc":"Euler characteristic for Bring's surface is −6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.covering_degree_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.covering_degree_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The covering has degree 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.covering_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.covering_degree","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L63-L63","doc":"(5c) Degree of the covering π : Σ₄ → P(V). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.total_ramification_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.total_ramification_eq","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Total ramification = 14. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.total_ramification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.total_ramification","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L59-L59","doc":"(5b) Total ramification from Riemann–Hurwitz. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.branch_points_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.branch_points_eq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L57-L57","doc":"There are exactly 6 branch points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.branch_points","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.branch_points","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L55-L55","doc":"(5a) Number of branch points in the geometric descent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.euler_char_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.euler_char_eq","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Euler characteristic matches genus formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.euler_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.euler_char","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L51-L51","doc":"(4) Euler characteristic = −6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.yekutieli_lifting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.yekutieli_lifting","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L49-L49","doc":"(3) Yekutieli lifting: the obstruction lies in H²(Σ₄, Z(SU_q(2))) =\nH²(Σ₄, ℤ/2) ≅ ℤ/2 (NOT 0 — closed orientable surface), so it is not\nforced to vanish. This field only encodes numPatches > 0 and does NOT\nencode the vanishing; an earlier comment claiming H² = 0 was false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.numPatches","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.numPatches","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Number of patches in a good cover of Σ₄. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.observability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.observability","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L42-L42","doc":"(2) Observability: Ad(A) ≅ V₂ (spin-1, dim 3), so Hom(𝟙, Ad(A)) = 0\nby the quantum Schur lemma (dim ≠ 1 ⟹ no trivial summand). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.adjReprDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.adjReprDim","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Dimension of the adjoint representation Ad(A) as a Rep(SU_q(2)) module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.quantum_universe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.quantum_universe","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L37-L37","doc":"(1) Quantum universe: the Woronowicz 3D calculus ⟹ dim(𝔤) = 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.lieAlgDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.lieAlgDim","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Dimension of the Lie algebra (= dim of the Woronowicz calculus Ω¹(A)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.genus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.genus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L33-L33","doc":"genus = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.genus","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Genus of the underlying surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.BringsIsQOU","kind":"structure","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-is-qou.lean#L18-L65","doc":"**QOU verification data for Bring's surface**.\n\nA structure packaging the five conditions that make Bring's surface\na quantum observable universe:\n1. Quantum universe: C = Rep(SU_q(2)), A = O_q(SU(2)), Woronowicz calculus\n2. Observability: Hom(1, Ad(A)) = 0 (quantum Schur lemma)\n3. Yekutieli lifting: brane tower satisfies lifting condition\n4. Euler characteristic: χ(A) = tr(id_A) = 2 − 2g = −6\n5. Geometric descent: 6 branch points, total ramification 14\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §5-brings-surface/brings-is-qou ","signatureChunk":0}]}